":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"The answer covers the central requested facts. It identifies cash collateral of 115% for undelivered securities, applies the percentage to the value of those undelivered securities rather than the whole order or basket, and says 115% is not universal. However, it omits several key points. It never mentions the 105% rate found in some reviewed forms, including the 'at least 105%' iShares terms in the Custodian section, which is the main evidence that the rate is not universal. Its 'up to 115%' wording also mischaracterizes the reviewed text, which describes 115% as typical and 105% in some forms, not 115% as a ceiling. Finally, it leaves out that the AP remains liable for any shortfall if the fund buys the missing securities itself.\"}","ttft_ms":2266,"type":"result","duration_ms":4481,"uuid":"ecb1ab9d-673e-418d-bb9f-5297b587ac88","ttft_stream_ms":614,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":614,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
